/**
@defgroup core Core
@brief Application and main loop, window, keyboard/mouse/gamepad input, action mapping, events,
fixed timestep, logging and assertions.

The lowest engine layer. Everything else builds on it, and it depends only on GLFW, OpenGL (through
GLAD) and spdlog. See @ref core_guide for an explanation of how the pieces work together.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/core/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup renderer Renderer
@brief 2D camera (rotation, parallax, shake), batched quad, sprite and text rendering, sprite
sheets and animation, render targets and post-processing, OpenGL wrappers.

Builds on @ref core. The camera, sprite sheet layout and animation player do not use OpenGL and
are unit-tested; Renderer2D and the wrappers need a current OpenGL 3.3 context. See
@ref renderer_guide for how batching works and how the pieces fit together.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/renderer/`.
*/

/**
@defgroup assets Assets
@brief Loading each texture, shader and font file once, with hot reloading.

Builds on @ref renderer. See the asset cache section of @ref renderer_guide.

Public headers live in `include/astra2d/assets/`.
*/

/**
@namespace astra2d
@brief All public engine types and functions.

Implementation details live in `astra2d::detail` and are not part of the API.
*/
